      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I was going to suggest reading the log file, but the usr_ is only grabbable if the home world instance would be owned by the player.\n\nWhen you log in with an avatar, when is the json file updated? Maybe you can scrape out a temporary work-around. Either compare the modified time of the avatar being changed into, or changed out of depending on when the files are written.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-02-07T07:45:07.670Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Documentation on OSC indicates that to get a list of parameters to parse the ~\\AppData\\LocalLow\\VRChat\\VRChat\\OSC\\{userId}\\Avatars\\{avatarId}.json file, and that a message is sent to /avatar/change that includes the avatarId when an avatar is changed\n\nIt does not appear that userId is exposed however, and while on a single-user machine this will always be the only folder in the OSC\\ folder, on machines used by multiple users this is not correct, making it impossible to be sure the correct {avatarId}.json is being loaded, particularly in the case of public avatars that both could have used at different times, and may  have different contents.  (This is relevant in particular in the case of face tracking)",
